.TH learn "" "Command"
.SH NAME
learn \- computer-aided instruction
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBlearn [\-\fIdirectory\fB] [\fIsubject \fB[\fIlesson \fB[\fIspeed\fB]]]\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
learn -- computer-aided instruction
Usage:	learn [ -directory ] [ subject [ lesson [ speed ] ] ]
If you do not know which subject or lesson you want,
type 'learn' and you will be guided from there.
.HE
.B learn
runs a computer-aided-instruction script that teaches the student
about
.I subject
by presenting a series of lessons and checking the student's typed
responses.
.PP
If invoked with no
.I subject
argument,
.B learn
lists the available subjects, read from
.B lib/subjects
under its lesson directory, and prompts
.BR "Enter subject ?" .
.PP
Once a
.I subject
is known,
.B learn
may also be given a
.I lesson
name within that subject, and a
.I speed
rating from 0 through 10 (values outside that range are forced to 10)
that controls how lessons of varying difficulty are chosen next; a
correct answer raises the rating by one, an incorrect one lowers it by
four.
.IP \fB\-\fIdirectory\fR
Use
.I directory
as the root of the lesson library, in place of the default,
.BR /usr/learn .
.PP
While working a lesson, the student may type
.B bye
in response to an incorrect-answer prompt to end the session
immediately.
.SH FILES
.DS
.ta 24n
\fB/usr/learn\fR	default lesson-library root
\fB/usr/learn/lib/subjects\fR	list of available subjects
\fB/usr/learn/lib/\fIsubject\fR	lessons for \fIsubject\fR
\fB/usr/learn/play\fR	student's scratch work area
.DE
.SH NOTES
.B learn
must be installed set-user-ID to the owner of
.BR /usr/learn/play ,
since it creates and removes a scratch directory there on the
student's behalf, and drops the privilege once the area is set up.
